            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0538" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg490"/>

                <head>No. 288.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 4, 1876</date>.
                        (Received December 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 449.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: General Concha has at last carried his
                    point and succeeded in making a set speech in the senate on the conduct of the
                    war in Cuba, in support of his recent motion reported in my No. 445. His speech
                    was in the main, a defense of his own late unfortunate command in Cuba, when the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">trocha</hi> was passed and Las Villas invaded with
                    such disastrous results by the insurgent forces.</p>
                <p>Mr. Calderon y Collantes replied, dwelling with much force and some bitterness on
                    the incidents of that campaign, which seems to be a sore point with the Marquis
                    de la Habana. The minister of war made a few remarks in answer to allusions, and
                    the debate was adjourned over until to-day.</p>
                <p>I send you copy of the Gaceta’s appendix with the report of the proceedings, and
                    also append translation of the remarks of the general and the minister
                    concerning the relations between Spain and the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. AUGUSTUS ADEE.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d288-a1.xml" xpointer="d288-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
